UPDATE stories
SET
  summary = replace(CASE story_key
    WHEN 'ai-futures-openai' THEN '- OpenAI launched AI Futures, a blog about how transformative AI could reshape society.\n- Its focus includes governance, economic power, and individual freedom rather than a new model release.\n- The series matters because it puts institutional consequences alongside technical progress in OpenAI''s public debate.'
    WHEN 'google-search-learning-tools' THEN '- Google collected five Search-based study approaches for students returning to class.\n- The guidance covers classwork and standardized-test preparation using familiar Search tools.\n- It frames existing features as a practical study workflow instead of announcing a separate education product.'
    WHEN 'huggingface-asr-benchmark' THEN '- Hugging Face examines how speech-recognition systems can be optimized around benchmarks.\n- The topic asks readers to look beyond a reported score when comparing evaluation results.\n- Its practical value is a clearer view of how benchmark targets can shape development and conclusions.'
    WHEN 'venturebeat-rob-strechay' THEN '- VentureBeat appointed Rob Strechay as its first Lead Analyst and a founding research analyst.\n- His remit covers enterprise AI infrastructure, orchestration, security, observability, and deployment.\n- The expanded research is aimed at technical leaders making production AI decisions.'
    WHEN 'nvidia-nemotron-langchain' THEN '- NVIDIA says LangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for Nemotron 3 Ultra.\n- The company reports stronger open-model accuracy, higher throughput, and lower-cost deployment.\n- Readers should treat those performance claims as vendor-reported because the candidate has no benchmark table.'
  END, '\\n', char(10)),
  summary_detailed = replace(CASE story_key
    WHEN 'ai-futures-openai' THEN 'OpenAI launched AI Futures as a blog about how transformative AI could reshape society. The publication concentrates on governance, the distribution of power, economic change, and individual freedom rather than announcing a specific model or product. That makes it a forum for considering consequences that sit outside a model''s technical performance.\n\nFor readers, the useful signal is that OpenAI is placing institutional questions alongside capability discussions. Future posts may clarify how the company connects these broad issues to its own policy positions, research priorities, and product choices. Until then, the launch is best understood as a public agenda for examining AI''s societal direction.'
    WHEN 'google-search-learning-tools' THEN 'Google''s back-to-school guidance collects five ways students can use Search tools for regular classwork and standardized-test preparation. The post packages familiar capabilities into a study-oriented workflow rather than announcing a standalone education product or a new model feature.\n\nThe practical takeaway is to evaluate whether those tools reduce friction in research, revision, and planning without replacing careful source checking. The candidate does not identify every feature or provide outcome data, so readers should view it as a seasonal usage guide and assess which suggestions fit their own study routine.'
    WHEN 'huggingface-asr-benchmark' THEN 'Hugging Face published a piece on measuring benchmark optimization in speech recognition. The available metadata does not establish its methods, datasets, numerical results, or a particular recognizer, but it clearly centers on the relationship between a benchmark score and the development choices made to improve it.\n\nThat distinction matters when teams compare speech systems or select an evaluation suite. A strong score can be useful evidence, yet readers should also ask whether the benchmark reflects their real audio, languages, error costs, and deployment conditions. The post is therefore an evaluation signal, not proof of a new product capability.'
    WHEN 'venturebeat-rob-strechay' THEN 'VentureBeat appointed Rob Strechay as its first Lead Analyst to deepen its enterprise AI research. His coverage includes cloud and data infrastructure, platform engineering, DevOps orchestration, observability, and the overlap between AI and enterprise security. The company also cites his experience as a practitioner, product executive, and analyst.\n\nFor technical decision-makers, the change signals more research on the operational layer beneath production AI. VentureBeat plans coverage of agentic orchestration, reliability and evaluations, identity and security, infrastructure and compute, and context systems. The announcement describes the editorial expansion, not an independently verified assessment of those markets.'
    WHEN 'nvidia-nemotron-langchain' THEN 'NVIDIA says Nemotron 3 Ultra achieved strong results when used with LangChain''s Deep Agents harness, an agent orchestration platform. According to the announcement, LangChain tuned the harness for Nemotron and the combination reached the highest accuracy among open models while completing more tasks at higher throughput.\n\nThe claimed result could matter for teams weighing open-model agent stacks against closed alternatives, especially where throughput and operating cost are important. However, the candidate does not include benchmark names, scores, workloads, or the comparison baseline. Treat the figures as NVIDIA''s reported results and validate them on representative workflows before making deployment decisions.'
  END, '\\n', char(10))
WHERE edition_id = (SELECT id FROM editions WHERE edition_date = '2026-08-24')
  AND story_key IN (
    'ai-futures-openai',
    'google-search-learning-tools',
    'huggingface-asr-benchmark',
    'venturebeat-rob-strechay',
    'nvidia-nemotron-langchain'
  );
